!!! Text scanning, in Matrix.
!!!
!!! nil.std.text has the primitives this needs — index_of, substring, trim,
!!! to_lower — and they work from Matrix. What it does not have in a form
!!! Matrix can use is anything returning a collection: `split` gives back a
!!! `vec<text>`, and a Matrix page cannot index or measure an Ny generic. So
!!! the splitting lives here, over `array of text`, which Matrix owns.
!!!
!!! Every paragraph here is total: an index past the end gives "" rather than
!!! faulting, because this code reads whatever arrives on a socket and a
!!! malformed request is an ordinary Tuesday, not an exception.

book nilweb.text.scan

read nil.std.text


!!! --- Split on a one-or-more character separator.
!!! An empty separator gives back the whole input as one part.

public split-on receives input as text, separator as text returns array of text begin paragraph
    variable parts as array of text is []
    value width is nil.std.text::length with s being separator
    when width is less than 1 then
        append input to parts
        give parts
    end when

    variable rest as text is input
    repeat forever
        value cut is nil.std.text::index_of with s being rest, needle being separator
        when cut is less than 0 then
            append rest to parts
            stop repeating
        end when
        append (nil.std.text::substring with s being rest, start being 0, length being cut) to parts
        value after is cut plus width
        value remaining is (nil.std.text::length with s being rest) minus after
        set rest to nil.std.text::substring with s being rest, start being after, length being remaining
    end repeat
    give parts
end paragraph


!!! --- Everything before the first separator, or all of it if there is none.

public before-first receives input as text, separator as text returns text begin paragraph
    value cut is nil.std.text::index_of with s being input, needle being separator
    when cut is less than 0 then
        give input
    end when
    give nil.std.text::substring with s being input, start being 0, length being cut
end paragraph


!!! --- Everything after the first separator, or "" if there is none.

public after-first receives input as text, separator as text returns text begin paragraph
    value cut is nil.std.text::index_of with s being input, needle being separator
    when cut is less than 0 then
        give ""
    end when
    value after is cut plus (nil.std.text::length with s being separator)
    value remaining is (nil.std.text::length with s being input) minus after
    give nil.std.text::substring with s being input, start being after, length being remaining
end paragraph


!!! --- ASCII case-insensitive equality.
!!!
!!! HTTP field names are case-insensitive, and that is the only folding this
!!! framework does: paths, query keys and cookie names are all compared exactly.

public same-folded receives left as text, right as text returns boolean begin paragraph
    give (nil.std.text::to_lower with s being left) equals (nil.std.text::to_lower with s being right)
end paragraph


!!! --- Whether the text has anything in it once space is taken off both ends.

public is-blank receives input as text returns boolean begin paragraph
    give (nil.std.text::trim with s being input) equals ""
end paragraph
